{
  "_doc": "Where reported quantities are looked for, in priority order. Each entry is [property-set glob, property name]. IFC quantity sets (quantities.reported) are searched first, then property sets (psets), so standard BaseQuantities win over authoring-tool sets. Every Qto_*BaseQuantities name has its generic BaseQuantities twin (IFC4 exports such as the S09 sample house write only BaseQuantities). Within a kind, net names come before gross ones; a NetArea (NetSideArea) larger than the GrossArea (GrossSideArea) of the same set is impossible and skipped (measure.find_reported: Revit 2021 IFC4 writes a slab's whole surface as NetArea), and a reported area is checked against a clear plate's measured sides (an area contradiction). Add authoring tools here, not in code. Rooms (IfcSpace): floor_area, ceiling_area, wall_area, wall_area_net, room_perimeter. Revit's room Area is deliberately not a source: it follows a Revit setting (wall centre, core or finish). A member's length is Revit's Cut Length (the physical member, its extrusion) before PSet_Revit_Dimensions.Length (Revit's analytical length between nodes, longer at the supports; A-17).",
